{
  "_comment": "Stage 4 draft (Medium Register B) for Joker (2019) - REBUILT v2 (2026-06-18). All clip bindings re-anchored to frame-verified shots.json v2. SC REORDER: U13=Penny smother (01:21, source precedes transformation), U14=Becoming Joker transformation+stairway-dance (01:24-01:31), NEW U15=detective subway chase (01:33). Old U15-U19+U_outro renumbered U16-U20+U_outro. Silence lines: L24 bathroom (00:34:50), L42 stairway (01:30:45), L56 Joker-on-car (01:51:15). UNRELIABLE NARRATOR preserved: Sophie real pre-U10; U10 explicit reveal; U20 Arkham ambiguity. NOTE: detective-chase line L43 currently reads as a transition; Phase 3 may split long lines. v1 had ~14 mis-anchored bindings from transcript-only catalogue; v2 every binding frame-verified.",
  "project": "joker2019",
  "lines": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "line_id": "L01",
      "unit_id": "U01",
      "covers": [
        "3"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:02:50.0",
      "clip_end": "00:02:54.5",
      "narration": "A broken man in clown makeup, beaten in an alley and laughed at by the city.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "reaction",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      },
      "narrative_jump": true
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "line_id": "L02",
      "unit_id": "U01",
      "covers": [
        "5"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:08:40.0",
      "clip_end": "00:08:51.6",
      "narration": "All he wants is to be seen. This is the story of what a society can make, when it looks away from the people it has already broken.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "setup",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "line_id": "L03",
      "unit_id": "U01",
      "covers": [
        "12"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:32:18.0",
      "clip_end": "00:32:27.5",
      "narration": "I'm Serabudabu, and today we're going inside Joker - twenty-nineteen, Todd Phillips' portrait of one man's slow collapse.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "action",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      },
      "narrative_jump": true
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "line_id": "L04",
      "unit_id": "U02",
      "covers": [
        "1"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:01:10.0",
      "clip_end": "00:01:20.8",
      "narration": "Arthur Fleck scrapes by as a party clown. We meet him at a mirror, forcing a smile up with his fingers while a single tear cuts through the paint.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "setup",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "line_id": "L05",
      "unit_id": "U02",
      "covers": [
        "1"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:01:21.0",
      "clip_end": "00:01:31.8",
      "narration": "He carries a condition that makes him laugh uncontrollably when he is frightened or in pain - the very opposite of joy, a laugh that sounds like choking.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "reveal",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "line_id": "L06",
      "unit_id": "U02",
      "covers": [
        "2"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:02:20.6",
      "clip_end": "00:02:29.1",
      "narration": "This is Gotham City, the early eighties. A garbage strike has buried the streets, super-rats roam the gutters, and a sick, angry city is quietly turning on itself.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "setup",
        "requires_visual": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "line_id": "L07",
      "unit_id": "U02",
      "covers": [
        "3"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:02:57.0",
      "clip_end": "00:03:06.5",
      "narration": "On the street, teenagers steal his sign and lure him into an alley, where they beat him on the ground for fun and leave him in the trash.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "action",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "line_id": "L08",
      "unit_id": "U03",
      "covers": [
        "4"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:05:50.0",
      "clip_end": "00:05:57.9",
      "narration": "Once a week a city social worker checks on him. She tracks his seven medications and asks, wearily, the same questions she always does.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "dialogue",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "line_id": "L09",
      "unit_id": "U03",
      "covers": [
        "4"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:06:18.0",
      "clip_end": "00:06:30.0",
      "narration": "She reads his journal aloud - a joke book that doubles as a diary, where punchlines sit beside something far darker.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "discovery",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "line_id": "L10",
      "unit_id": "U03",
      "covers": [
        "4"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:06:18.0",
      "clip_end": "00:06:30.0",
      "narration": "One scrawled line says it all: I just hope my death makes more cents than my life. He has already imagined the end; he is only waiting.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "discovery",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "line_id": "L11",
      "unit_id": "U03",
      "covers": [
        "4"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:07:15.8",
      "clip_end": "00:07:25.3",
      "narration": "Then the worker tells him the city has cut their funding. The sessions are over, and so is his access to medication.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "dialogue",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "line_id": "L12",
      "unit_id": "U03",
      "covers": [
        "4"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:07:15.8",
      "clip_end": "00:07:25.3",
      "narration": "The one thin support holding him together is pulled away, quietly, by people who will never see his face again. Nobody listens, she says. Nobody ever does.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "reaction",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "line_id": "L13",
      "unit_id": "U03",
      "covers": [
        "5"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:08:54.5",
      "clip_end": "00:09:04.9",
      "narration": "On the bus one day, a laughing fit seizes him completely, and strangers stare as he chokes on a sound he cannot stop or explain.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "reaction",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "line_id": "L14",
      "unit_id": "U03",
      "covers": [
        "6"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:12:00.0",
      "clip_end": "00:12:09.9",
      "narration": "At home he cares for his frail mother, Penny. He bathes her, feeds her, and they watch television together like a closed little world of two.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "emotion",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "line_id": "L15",
      "unit_id": "U03",
      "covers": [
        "6"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:12:40.0",
      "clip_end": "00:12:54.4",
      "narration": "Penny calls him Happy and insists he was put on earth to spread joy. She raised him to wear a smile no matter what - the mask he has never been allowed to set down.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "dialogue",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Penny"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "line_id": "L16",
      "unit_id": "U04",
      "covers": [
        "6"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:12:00.0",
      "clip_end": "00:12:09.9",
      "narration": "Every night they watch the Murray Franklin show, Arthur's favorite - a warm, glittering world that feels like the family he never had.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "setup",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "line_id": "L17",
      "unit_id": "U04",
      "covers": [
        "7"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:13:20.0",
      "clip_end": "00:13:27.1",
      "narration": "Murray is everything Arthur is not: admired, listened to, loved without having to beg for it.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "setup",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Murray"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "line_id": "L18",
      "unit_id": "U04",
      "covers": [
        "7"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:14:30.0",
      "clip_end": "00:14:44.4",
      "narration": "He drifts into a daydream. Murray calls him out of the audience, embraces him like a father, and says he would give it all up for a son like him.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "reveal",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "line_id": "L19",
      "unit_id": "U04",
      "covers": [
        "7"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:15:10.0",
      "clip_end": "00:15:21.2",
      "narration": "It is a fantasy about one simple thing - to be seen, and wanted, by someone who matters. The whole tragedy is folded into that small wish.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "reveal",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "line_id": "L20",
      "unit_id": "U05",
      "covers": [
        "8"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:23:10.0",
      "clip_end": "00:23:17.0",
      "narration": "At work, the clown Randall slips Arthur a gun for protection - now Arthur holds it at home, a loaded thing that will not stay hidden.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "action",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "line_id": "L21",
      "unit_id": "U05",
      "covers": [
        "8"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:23:18.0",
      "clip_end": "00:23:33.0",
      "narration": "Arthur takes it, uneasy. In a world that keeps hurting him, even a small piece of power feels, for a moment, like safety.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "reaction",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "line_id": "L22",
      "unit_id": "U05",
      "covers": [
        "9"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:19:50.0",
      "clip_end": "00:19:58.0",
      "narration": "In his building he meets Sophie, a single mother down the hall - the first person in a long time who looks at him without flinching.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "setup",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Sophie"
      },
      "narrative_jump": true
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "line_id": "L23",
      "unit_id": "U05",
      "covers": [
        "9"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:20:05.0",
      "clip_end": "00:20:21.0",
      "narration": "She is sharp and warm, and when she mimes a gun to her own head about their grim building, Arthur lights up. Here, at last, is someone who seems to get him.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "dialogue",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Sophie"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 24,
      "line_id": "L24",
      "unit_id": "U05",
      "covers": [
        "9"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:20:25.0",
      "clip_end": "00:20:38.0",
      "narration": "In a life this lonely, she becomes his one fragile thread of hope - hold on to that.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "emotion",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 25,
      "line_id": "L25",
      "unit_id": "U06",
      "covers": [
        "10"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:28:18.0",
      "clip_end": "00:28:23.9",
      "narration": "Arthur entertains a ward of sick children, doing his best to make them laugh.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "action",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 26,
      "line_id": "L26",
      "unit_id": "U06",
      "covers": [
        "10"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:28:46.0",
      "clip_end": "00:28:54.7",
      "narration": "But the gun slips from his costume and clatters onto the floor in front of everyone. He is fired on the spot, humiliated again.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "action",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 27,
      "line_id": "L27",
      "unit_id": "U06",
      "covers": [
        "11"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:30:39.0",
      "clip_end": "00:30:47.4",
      "narration": "Late that night on the subway, three drunk Wall Street men corner him and begin to torment him for sport.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "action",
        "requires_visual": true
      },
      "montage": [
        {
          "clip_start": "00:30:39.0",
          "clip_end": "00:30:41.8",
          "play_duration": 1.94
        },
        {
          "clip_start": "00:30:41.8",
          "clip_end": "00:30:44.0",
          "play_duration": 1.524
        },
        {
          "clip_start": "00:30:44.0",
          "clip_end": "00:30:47.4",
          "play_duration": 2.356
        }
      ],
      "total_visual_duration": 5.82
    },
    {
      "id": 28,
      "line_id": "L28",
      "unit_id": "U07",
      "covers": [
        "11"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:31:05.0",
      "clip_end": "00:31:12.6",
      "narration": "His laughter erupts at the worst possible moment, and the men close in to beat him.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "action",
        "requires_visual": true
      },
      "montage": [
        {
          "clip_start": "00:31:04.0",
          "clip_end": "00:31:08.2",
          "play_duration": 2.116
        },
        {
          "clip_start": "00:31:08.2",
          "clip_end": "00:31:10.2",
          "play_duration": 1.007
        },
        {
          "clip_start": "00:31:10.2",
          "clip_end": "00:31:12.6",
          "play_duration": 1.209
        }
      ],
      "total_visual_duration": 4.332
    },
    {
      "id": 29,
      "line_id": "L29",
      "unit_id": "U07",
      "covers": [
        "12"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:32:32.0",
      "clip_end": "00:32:40.0",
      "narration": "And Arthur shoots them. Two go down in the car; then he hunts the last man up the stairs and finishes him in cold blood.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "action",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      },
      "montage": [
        {
          "clip_start": "00:32:32.0",
          "clip_end": "00:32:34.0",
          "play_duration": 1.623
        },
        {
          "clip_start": "00:32:34.0",
          "clip_end": "00:32:37.0",
          "play_duration": 2.434
        },
        {
          "clip_start": "00:32:37.0",
          "clip_end": "00:32:40.0",
          "play_duration": 2.435
        }
      ],
      "total_visual_duration": 6.492
    },
    {
      "id": 30,
      "line_id": "L30",
      "unit_id": "U07",
      "covers": [
        "12"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:33:27.0",
      "clip_end": "00:33:38.2",
      "narration": "For the first time in his life, he has taken control. He flees into a public bathroom - and what happens next is the film's quiet hinge.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "transition",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 31,
      "line_id": "L31",
      "unit_id": "U08",
      "covers": [
        "13"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:34:50.0",
      "clip_end": "00:34:56.0",
      "narration": "",
      "narration_silence_seconds": 22.0
    },
    {
      "id": 32,
      "line_id": "L32",
      "unit_id": "U09",
      "covers": [
        "14"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:36:10.0",
      "clip_end": "00:36:20.4",
      "narration": "The killings electrify Gotham. A masked clown who gunned down three Wall Street men becomes a folk hero to a city sick of the rich.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "reveal",
        "requires_visual": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 33,
      "line_id": "L33",
      "unit_id": "U09",
      "covers": [
        "15"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:40:10.0",
      "clip_end": "00:40:20.8",
      "narration": "Sophie comes to Arthur, and the two fall into an easy intimacy. For a while, his fantasy and his life seem to finally line up.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "emotion",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 34,
      "line_id": "L34",
      "unit_id": "U09",
      "covers": [
        "16"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:42:40.0",
      "clip_end": "00:42:49.5",
      "narration": "He finally lands a stand-up spot - but on stage, the laughing fit wrecks the set, and the room turns on him.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "action",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 35,
      "line_id": "L35",
      "unit_id": "U09",
      "covers": [
        "17"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:00:00.0",
      "clip_end": "01:00:09.5",
      "narration": "Worse, Murray plays the tape on his show and mocks Arthur for a laughing studio audience - his idol, humiliating him on national television.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "reveal",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Murray"
      },
      "narrative_jump": true
    },
    {
      "id": 36,
      "line_id": "L36",
      "unit_id": "U10",
      "covers": [
        "18"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:49:10.0",
      "clip_end": "00:49:20.8",
      "narration": "Then Arthur finds a letter his mother wrote, never sent. In it, Penny claims that Thomas Wayne - the billionaire now running for mayor - is Arthur's secret father.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "discovery",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 37,
      "line_id": "L37",
      "unit_id": "U10",
      "covers": [
        "18"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:50:23.5",
      "clip_end": "00:50:34.3",
      "narration": "She writes of Wayne as a great and powerful man she once loved, when she worked in his household years ago.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "dialogue",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Penny"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 38,
      "line_id": "L38",
      "unit_id": "U10",
      "covers": [
        "18"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:50:23.5",
      "clip_end": "00:50:34.3",
      "narration": "There were letters, she says - many of them, over many years, none ever answered. For Arthur it lands like a lifeline: maybe he belongs to someone after all.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "reaction",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 39,
      "line_id": "L39",
      "unit_id": "U10",
      "covers": [
        "19"
      ],
      "clip_start": "00:53:40.0",
      "clip_end": "00:53:47.1",
      "narration": "He travels to Wayne Manor, meeting a young Bruce through the gate before Alfred coldly turns him away.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "action",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 40,
      "line_id": "L40",
      "unit_id": "U10",
      "covers": [
        "20"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:05:30.4",
      "clip_end": "01:05:40.8",
      "narration": "When he finally corners Thomas Wayne in a theater bathroom, the answer is brutal: Wayne denies everything, says Penny adopted him, and calls her delusional.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "dialogue",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Wayne"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 41,
      "line_id": "L41",
      "unit_id": "U10",
      "covers": [
        "21"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:06:30.0",
      "clip_end": "01:06:39.9",
      "narration": "Reeling, Arthur lets himself into Sophie's apartment - and the floor drops out from under the whole film.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "transition",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 42,
      "line_id": "L42",
      "unit_id": "U10",
      "covers": [
        "22"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:07:30.0",
      "clip_end": "01:07:38.8",
      "narration": "Sophie was never his. She is a frightened stranger, asking the intruder in her home to leave, while she shields her child.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "dialogue",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Sophie"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 43,
      "line_id": "L43",
      "unit_id": "U10",
      "covers": [
        "22"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:07:39.0",
      "clip_end": "01:07:47.8",
      "narration": "Every tender moment we watched between them happened only in Arthur's mind. The relationship that anchored him, that anchored us, was a delusion all along.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "reveal",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 44,
      "line_id": "L44",
      "unit_id": "U11",
      "covers": [
        "23"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:11:04.6",
      "clip_end": "01:11:18.2",
      "narration": "Desperate for the truth, Arthur talks his way into Arkham State Hospital and steals his mother's old case file.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "discovery",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 45,
      "line_id": "L45",
      "unit_id": "U11",
      "covers": [
        "23"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:11:04.6",
      "clip_end": "01:11:18.2",
      "narration": "The papers say he was adopted thirty years ago. As a small child he was chained to a radiator, starved, and beaten - while Penny stood by and let it happen.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "discovery",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 46,
      "line_id": "L46",
      "unit_id": "U11",
      "covers": [
        "23"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:13:30.0",
      "clip_end": "01:13:42.4",
      "narration": "The head trauma from that abuse, the file says, is the source of his uncontrollable laugh. His mother's own records note a history of delusion and psychosis.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "discovery",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 47,
      "line_id": "L47",
      "unit_id": "U11",
      "covers": [
        "23"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:13:30.0",
      "clip_end": "01:13:42.4",
      "narration": "And if Sophie was never real, we can no longer trust anything we have been shown - and neither can he. Every certainty about who he is quietly comes apart.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "reaction",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 48,
      "line_id": "L48",
      "unit_id": "U12",
      "covers": [
        "24"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:17:48.0",
      "clip_end": "01:17:52.0",
      "narration": "His old coworkers Randall and Gary come to check on him after the firing.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "dialogue",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 49,
      "line_id": "L49",
      "unit_id": "U12",
      "covers": [
        "24"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:18:00.0",
      "clip_end": "01:18:07.9",
      "narration": "Arthur kills Randall - cold, sudden, without the laughter this time. A choice, not a fit.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "action",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 50,
      "line_id": "L50",
      "unit_id": "U12",
      "covers": [
        "24"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:18:30.0",
      "clip_end": "01:18:39.5",
      "narration": "He lets the small, kind Gary go unharmed, and the gentleness of that mercy is somehow the most frightening thing of all.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "reaction",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 51,
      "line_id": "L51",
      "unit_id": "U12",
      "covers": [
        "24"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:18:55.0",
      "clip_end": "01:19:02.1",
      "narration": "It is the first life he takes by choice, and it does not shake him. Something in him has gone quiet and certain.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "emotion",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 52,
      "line_id": "L52",
      "unit_id": "U13",
      "covers": [
        "25"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:21:00.0",
      "clip_end": "01:21:09.9",
      "narration": "Then he visits his mother in the hospital, sits at her bedside, and tells her she gave him a terrible life and a lie to live inside.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "dialogue",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 53,
      "line_id": "L53",
      "unit_id": "U13",
      "covers": [
        "25"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:21:25.0",
      "clip_end": "01:21:30.5",
      "narration": "Quietly, he smothers her with a pillow. The last tie to who Arthur Fleck was is gone.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "action",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 54,
      "line_id": "L54",
      "unit_id": "U14",
      "covers": [
        "26"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:24:30.0",
      "clip_end": "01:24:37.1",
      "narration": "He dyes his hair green and paints the face we have been waiting for. Arthur Fleck is disappearing, and something new is stepping forward.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "transition",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 55,
      "line_id": "L55",
      "unit_id": "U14",
      "covers": [
        "26"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:26:30.0",
      "clip_end": "01:26:39.5",
      "narration": "For the first time, the face in the mirror looks certain. Arthur dances down a long flight of stairs as if gravity has finally let him go.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "emotion",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 56,
      "line_id": "L56",
      "unit_id": "U14",
      "covers": [
        "26"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:30:45.0",
      "clip_end": "01:30:51.0",
      "narration": "",
      "narration_silence_seconds": 22.0
    },
    {
      "id": 57,
      "line_id": "L57",
      "unit_id": "U15",
      "covers": [
        "27"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:33:00.0",
      "clip_end": "01:33:07.5",
      "narration": "Two detectives corner him on a subway car packed with rioters in clown masks.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "action",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 58,
      "line_id": "L58",
      "unit_id": "U15",
      "covers": [
        "27"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:33:25.0",
      "clip_end": "01:33:35.5",
      "narration": "He pulls on a mask of his own and melts into the crowd, slipping away in the chaos he helped create.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "action",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      },
      "montage": [
        {
          "clip_start": "01:33:25.6",
          "clip_end": "01:33:28.5",
          "play_duration": 1.539
        },
        {
          "clip_start": "01:33:28.7",
          "clip_end": "01:33:32.1",
          "play_duration": 1.804
        },
        {
          "clip_start": "01:33:32.1",
          "clip_end": "01:33:35.5",
          "play_duration": 1.805
        }
      ],
      "total_visual_duration": 5.148
    },
    {
      "id": 59,
      "line_id": "L59",
      "unit_id": "U16",
      "covers": [
        "28"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:35:19.2",
      "clip_end": "01:35:30.4",
      "narration": "Then an invitation arrives he could never have dreamed of. The Murray show wants the laughing clown as a guest - to put him on air and laugh at him.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "discovery",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 60,
      "line_id": "L60",
      "unit_id": "U16",
      "covers": [
        "29"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:38:40.0",
      "clip_end": "01:38:45.5",
      "narration": "He arrives as the Joker, and asks Murray to introduce him by that name.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "dialogue",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 61,
      "line_id": "L61",
      "unit_id": "U16",
      "covers": [
        "30"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:41:10.0",
      "clip_end": "01:41:16.3",
      "narration": "On live television, in front of the whole city, he confesses to the subway killings.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "reveal",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 62,
      "line_id": "L62",
      "unit_id": "U16",
      "covers": [
        "31"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:44:16.5",
      "clip_end": "01:44:29.7",
      "narration": "And here the film says its hardest thing out loud. Arthur asks what a society expects when it abandons people and grinds them down - then acts shocked at what they become.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "dialogue",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 63,
      "line_id": "L63",
      "unit_id": "U16",
      "covers": [
        "31"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:44:16.5",
      "clip_end": "01:44:29.7",
      "narration": "If it were me dying on the sidewalk, he says, you'd walk right over me. The rich are decent; the rest are disposable - and everybody just screams at each other.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "dialogue",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 64,
      "line_id": "L64",
      "unit_id": "U16",
      "covers": [
        "31"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:44:40.0",
      "clip_end": "01:44:45.0",
      "narration": "The recognition he begged for all his life, he now seizes by force, in front of millions.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "reaction",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 65,
      "line_id": "L65",
      "unit_id": "U17",
      "covers": [
        "32"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:45:00.0",
      "clip_end": "01:45:05.9",
      "narration": "Murray scolds him for self-pity and tells him he will get exactly what he deserves.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "dialogue",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Murray"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 66,
      "line_id": "L66",
      "unit_id": "U17",
      "covers": [
        "32"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:45:40.0",
      "clip_end": "01:45:50.8",
      "narration": "So the Joker shows him what that means. He shoots Murray dead on live television, then turns calmly to the lens and wishes the city a good night.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "action",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 67,
      "line_id": "L67",
      "unit_id": "U18",
      "covers": [
        "33"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:47:10.0",
      "clip_end": "01:47:18.3",
      "narration": "The broadcast lights the fuse. Gotham erupts - masked rioters flood the streets, smashing and burning the city that ignored them.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "action",
        "requires_visual": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 68,
      "line_id": "L68",
      "unit_id": "U18",
      "covers": [
        "33"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:47:35.0",
      "clip_end": "01:47:44.0",
      "narration": "Arthur, arrested in the chaos, is pulled from the wreck and lifted up by the mob like a saint of the gutter.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "action",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 69,
      "line_id": "L69",
      "unit_id": "U18",
      "covers": [
        "34"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:48:30.0",
      "clip_end": "01:48:37.5",
      "narration": "And in an alley behind a theater, the riot reaches the one family Gotham always treated as untouchable.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "transition",
        "requires_visual": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 70,
      "line_id": "L70",
      "unit_id": "U18",
      "covers": [
        "34"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:49:50.0",
      "clip_end": "01:49:58.0",
      "narration": "A clown-masked gunman shoots Thomas Wayne and his wife dead on the wet pavement, her pearls scattering across the ground.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "action",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Wayne"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 71,
      "line_id": "L71",
      "unit_id": "U18",
      "covers": [
        "34"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:50:00.0",
      "clip_end": "01:50:07.0",
      "narration": "He leaves their young son Bruce alive between his parents bodies. Out of the chaos Arthur unleashed, another legend is born in the dark.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "reaction",
        "requires_visual": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 72,
      "line_id": "L72",
      "unit_id": "U19",
      "covers": [
        "35"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:51:15.0",
      "clip_end": "01:51:28.0",
      "narration": "The rioters drag the Joker up onto a wrecked police car. Bloodied and dazed, he rises to find a whole city that finally, monstrously, sees him.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "reveal",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 73,
      "line_id": "L73",
      "unit_id": "U19",
      "covers": [
        "35"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:51:15.0",
      "clip_end": "01:51:28.0",
      "narration": "",
      "narration_silence_seconds": 13.0
    },
    {
      "id": 74,
      "line_id": "L74",
      "unit_id": "U20",
      "covers": [
        "36"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:53:14.0",
      "clip_end": "01:53:21.0",
      "narration": "We end with the Joker back in Arkham, talking quietly to a doctor, laughing at a joke he says she would not understand.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "dialogue",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      },
      "montage": [
        {
          "clip_start": "01:53:14.0",
          "clip_end": "01:53:17.1",
          "play_duration": 2.705
        },
        {
          "clip_start": "01:53:17.1",
          "clip_end": "01:53:19.8",
          "play_duration": 2.356
        },
        {
          "clip_start": "01:53:19.8",
          "clip_end": "01:53:21.0",
          "play_duration": 1.047
        }
      ],
      "total_visual_duration": 6.108
    },
    {
      "id": 75,
      "line_id": "L75",
      "unit_id": "U20",
      "covers": [
        "36"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:53:15.0",
      "clip_end": "01:53:27.8",
      "narration": "The film never tells us how much of what we saw was real and how much lived only in his head - and it refuses to. That uncertainty is the whole point.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "reveal",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 76,
      "line_id": "L76",
      "unit_id": "U20",
      "covers": [
        "37"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:55:18.0",
      "clip_end": "01:55:30.0",
      "narration": "He walks away down a bright corridor, and a trail of fresh bloody footprints follows him out. We are left to wonder what he has just done, and where this ends.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "reveal",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 77,
      "line_id": "L77",
      "unit_id": "U_outro",
      "covers": [
        "37"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:54:50.0",
      "clip_end": "01:55:04.8",
      "narration": "Joker is a portrait of a man failed at every turn, and a warning about a world that creates its own monsters and then recoils from them.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "transition",
        "requires_visual": true,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 78,
      "line_id": "L78",
      "unit_id": "U_outro",
      "covers": [
        "37"
      ],
      "clip_start": "01:54:50.0",
      "clip_end": "01:55:04.8",
      "narration": "It does not excuse him - it asks us to look. Thanks for watching: if this one hit you, hit like and subscribe for more deep dives like this.",
      "claim": {
        "type": "narration",
        "requires_visual": false,
        "subject": "Arthur"
      }
    }
  ]
}